Author:     Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
AuthorDate: Sun Aug 9 23:15:43 2026 +0300
Commit:     Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Sun Nov 15 18:07:06 2026 -0500

    iommu: qcom_iommu: support the short-descriptor pagetable format
    
    Original integration rationale and historical observations follow. These
    observations do not qualify hardware on this refreshed base.
    
    The MSM8974-generation QSMMU does not walk the LPAE tables this driver
    hardcodes: every access faults with an access flag fault despite AF
    being set in the descriptors, and with SCTLR.AFE cleared the walks still
    return garbage translations (observed on the APQ8074 dragonboard GPU,
    which locks up on its first ringbuffer fetch). The downstream kernel
    only ever used the short-descriptor format on MSM8974; its LPAE support
    was reserved for the newer APQ8084 IP / TZ revision.
    
    Introduce a per-instance configuration structure, selected through the
    of_device_id match data, carrying a pagetable format field and an AFE
    quirk flag. For the ARM_V7S format, program the ASID through CONTEXTIDR
    instead of the TTBR0 ASID field, reuse the MAIR register offsets for
    PRRR/NMRR, restrict the output address size to 32 bits and keep
    SCTLR.AFE disabled like the downstream driver does when the no_afe flag
    is set. No instance sets a configuration yet.
    
    Original integration AI credit: Claude:claude-fable-5.
    
    Refreshed from integration source
    e627f8707ea7b1ce29926062f65cb4ae4e8d9983. Current-base adaptation and
    host qualification used OpenAI Codex. Human review and new DCO
    certification remain pending.

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/Kconfig b/drivers/iommu/arm/Kconfig
index 5fac08b89dee..596e643961c3 100644
